+# Democratic peace numerical methods
+
+The canonical `methods.json` template is consumed by Python and native Rust. Its digest is frozen with all source and executable bindings before any registered period. It pins Python3.13.5, NumPy2.4.6, root2026100302 and129 deterministic child jobs:105 source predictions and independent permutation/bootstrap jobs for12 contrast components. Fixture tolerances for derived census metrics are absolute1e-12. These are premeasurement choices.
+
+Territorial means retain every complete history, including zero democratic territory. Clustering means condition on final democratic survival and preserve legitimate undefined values. Initial density0 is undefined; final extinction is undefined; neither is a model invalidity. First extinction can precede later democratic reemergence under persistent latent tags, so historical first-passage times do not determine final survival.
+
+Source inference requires all30 original histories complete, all100 precision histories complete and a readable audited source interval. Each100000-attempt prediction resamples30 precision histories with replacement. Clustering carries extinction masks through sampling, reports undefined draws and conditions on defined replicates. At least two surviving precision histories and10000 defined draws are required. All-extinction resamples are never replaced or assigned zero. Original-only registration never substitutes30 histories for100.
+
+Inclusive equal-tail p-values use plus-one correction. Exact interval maximization considers every predictive sample knot inside the closed source interval, both endpoints and every open gap. Open-gap tail counts are computed analytically, including adjacent floating-point endpoints with no representable midpoint; no favorable coarse grid is used. Holm correction retains all105 potential slots, using internal p1 for unavailable values while exporting null p-values and reasons. Scope with zero readable targets remains Unresolved.
+
+Primary and secondary contrasts each have six tests, independent group histories,100000 uniform pooled200-history permutations split100/100, and100000 independent within-group bootstrap draws. Permutation p-values use inclusive absolute differences and plus-one correction. Percentile intervals select sorted indices floor(.025×(B−1)) and ceil(.975×(B−1)); no interpolation changes the registered quantile rule. Holm at.05 applies separately to the two six-test families.
+
+Missing/invalid histories block registered inference. Constructed, partial, panicked and unavailable attempts remain in the key census. Complete-count and clustering-survivor/extinction denominators remain visible. Values outside finite bootstrap support are not impossible model events. Neither source matching nor these lattice contrasts establish historical democratic-peace causality or original executable/RNG identity.
+
+Python tests exercise fixed populations, unavailable source slots, atomic partial outcomes, extinction masks, first-passage availability, interval jumps/open gaps, multiplicity, independent contrasts, duplicate/nonfinite JSON and identity drift using deterministic small synthetic fixtures. Fixture draw overrides cannot enter a registered report.
