+# Democratic peace offline survey
+
+This package prepares and audits the prospective Cederman2001 reconstruction study. It never activates populations or freezes sources on import. No registered histories or measured scientific findings accompany implementation.
+
+Native Rust resolves every configuration from the printed2001 preset. Python supplies partial overrides and consumes the exact native resolved payload, never substitutes independently guessed defaults. Original108×30 histories and optional precision108×100 histories have disjoint fixed seeds. The runtime gate must select the entire original population or the entire original plus precision population before measurement. No alternative reading is included silently.
+
+Source extraction is in `extraction.py`; its figure table and report live in `docs/superpowers/specs/`. Audit every interval and readable mask before freeze. The105 source slots retain absent/overlap reasons, with three undefined density-zero exclusions outside the family. Source equivalence remains Unresolved.
+
+Run small deterministic Python fixtures with:
+
+```bash
+python3 -m unittest discover -s survey/democratic_peace -p 'test_*.py'
+```
+
+The analysis runtime is Python3.13.5 with NumPy2.4.6, reusing the existing scientific environment. No new scientific library is required. Reduced draws are only accepted by explicit bounded fixture manifests, and fixture reports are labeled synthetic_fixture. Registered source draws, permutation counts and contrast bootstrap counts remain100000.
+
+For preparation, `python3 -m survey.democratic_peace.manifest --source TABLE --output MANIFEST` creates a provisional original-only manifest. The explicit `--precision-registered` flag prepares both populations; it does not itself authorize a scientific run. `provenance.freeze_manifest` requires audited sources and all writers stopped. Fixture/probe builders and `bind_unregistered_manifest` preserve bounded nonregistered identities. The native recorder rejects oversized fixture/probe populations, unknown fields, duplicate keys, nonfinite values, provenance drift and interrupted appends.
+
+Native command contract: `--manifest PATH --resolved PATH --repo ROOT --validate-only` validates without world construction. Execution additionally requires `--out PATH --receipt PATH`. A build receipt binds actual binary, pre/post source inventories, commands, toolchains and both Cargo locks. The resolved export retains exact no-newline UTF8 array bytes in resolved_configs_json; its SHA binds the full decoded config payload. Raw rows retain one attempt per exact key with family/mode, canonical and sequential arm indices, resolved config, attempt context, full finite science output and five provenance identities.
+
+Do not run registered periods or analyze/resample a measured population until explicitly authorized with a frozen manifest. Runtime probes use seeds400000001 onward, remain separately classified, and cannot select scientific defaults or judges. Evidence belongs under the explicitly verified ignored `survey/out/democratic-peace-*` prefix; do not assume another prefix is ignored.
